# NATS JetStream: durable work queue with Pull Consumers

A durable `WorkQueuePolicy` stream (`JOBS`) and a shared Pull Consumer (`job-workers`) across two worker replicas using `github.com/nats-io/nats.go/jetstream`:

- `js-producer` publishes jobs on `jobs.<kind>` with `Nats-Msg-Id` deduplication headers, intentionally resending every 6th ID so you can see JetStream return `duplicate=true`.
- `js-worker` (2 replicas) pulls batches from `job-workers` (`AckExplicit`, `MaxDeliver: 3`, `AckWait: 5s`), calls `msg.NakWithDelay(500ms)` on delivery 1 of every 5th job, and `msg.Ack()`s finished jobs (which immediately deletes them from the WorkQueue stream).

## Try this

- Watch deduplication, retries, and balanced work distribution:
  ```sh
  bb up
  bb logs js-producer
  bb logs js-worker -f
  ```
- Open `bb serve`, click `nats`, and check **Streams & stats** to watch stream `JOBS` and consumer `job-workers` (`pending`, `ack`, `delivered`).

## Break this

- **Stop both workers while the producer keeps publishing:** Stop `js-worker-1` and `js-worker-2`, watch `JOBS` messages and `pending` grow in **Streams & stats**, then start the workers again — every queued job drains cleanly without loss.
- **Exceed `MaxDeliver`:** Edit `cmd/js-worker/main.go` to `NakWithDelay` unconditionally on a job and watch JetStream stop redelivering after attempt 3.
